<title>USA: Tyco sets March 18 vote on Mattel merger.</title>
<headline>Tyco sets March 18 vote on Mattel merger.</headline>
<dateline>MT. LAUREL, N.J. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tyco Toys Inc said Wednesday it had scheduled a special meeting of shareholders for March 18 to vote on a proposed merger with Mattel Inc .</p>
<p>The company said it had set a record date of February 7 for shareholders eligible to vote on the merger.</p>
<p>Tyco, which makes Sesame Street preschool toys, Magna Doodle drawing toys and Matchbox cars, and Mattel anounced in November they planned to merge in a $755 million stock deal.</p>
</text>
